@startuml
!theme cyborg
skinparam backgroundColor #111827
skinparam defaultFontColor #F3F4F6
allowmixing
title Proposed — Implementation view: logical owners to physical outputs
skinparam backgroundColor #111827
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

rectangle "Nine logical component owners\nIdentity / Presentation / Sharing / Applications\nCommunication / Work / Git / Workflow / Files" as L
package "Proposed source organization\nnot a claim these files exist" {
 rectangle "app/Modules/<Owner>\npublic contracts + owned implementation" as S
 rectangle "bootstrap / routes / config\nresources / migrations / ops templates" as C
}
artifact "IA-01 trusted application release\ncoordinated module code / resolved dependencies" as A
artifact "IA-02 UI/static outputs" as U
artifact "IA-03 ordered schema migrations" as D
artifact "IA-06 safe operating templates\nrelease manifest / prerequisite identities" as O
L --> S : implemented by owned source
S --> A : assembled into
C --> A : selected release inputs
A --> U : compatible output set
A --> D : compatible migration set
A --> O : identifies configuration / operating requirements
note bottom of A
 One coordinated release can realize several logical modules.
 Web/worker entry points share compatible release contracts.
 Untrusted workflow execution is not inside trusted app privilege by implication.
end note

@enduml